02:21:51.000 --> 02:22:39.000
"...nothing in this case ever made sense, and no one, it seems, played by the rules. Amanda Knox will always be remembered as someone who hung in the balance between sinner and saint, good and evil, and Meredith's murder will always be a mystery that was blurred by the headlines and lost in translation. One CBS reporter noted that the irony of this case is that the Italian authorities actually did a great job in that within three weeks of Meredith's murder, Rudy Guadar was identified and caught. It was when they refused to drop Amanda and Rafael as suspects that the problems began. Private investigator Bob Graham agreed, responding, the prosecution dug a hole so deep that they

