02:22:39.000 --> 02:23:33.000
couldn't get out of it, and pride, vanity, whatever it was, ensured they just kept digging. Rudy Guadar was released from prison in November 2021, having served 13 years of his 16-year sentence for Meredith Kercher's brutal sexual assault and murder. His lawyer told the press that Rudy had been adequately reeducated, while a lawyer for the Kircher family said the early release would renew the family's unspeakable suffering. Amanda voiced her opinion on Twitter, writing, Gwede holds a tremendous power to heal others harmed by his actions. He has the power to tell the truth, to take responsibility, to stop blaming me for the rape and murder of Meredith Kerger, which a wealth of evidence shows he committed alone.

